# SD
1. Company is a physical and systemic object.
2. Securities & Exchange Commission is a physical and environmental object.
3. Underwriter Group is a physical and environmental object.
4. Underwriter Group can be candidate or selected.
5. Blue-sky Law Set is an informatical and environmental object.
6. Fact Presentation is an informatical and systemic object.
7. Fact Presentation can be fair, presented or unfair.
8. State presented is initial.
9. Price of Stock Issue is an informatical and systemic object.
10. Price of Stock Issue can be fixed or preliminary.
11. State preliminary is initial.
12. Stock Issue is an informatical and systemic object.
13. Stock Issue can be compliant, new, offered or purchased.
14. State new is initial.
15. Advice is an informatical and systemic object.
16. Firm Commitment is an informatical and systemic object.
17. Registration Statement is an informatical and systemic object.
18. Registration Statement can be approved or pending.
19. State pending is initial.
20. Road Show is an informatical and systemic object.
21. Initial Public Offering is an informatical and systemic process.
22. Company, Securities & Exchange Commission, and Underwriter Group handle Initial Public Offering.
23. Initial Public Offering requires Blue-sky Law Set.
24. Initial Public Offering affects Fact Presentation, Price of Stock Issue, and Stock Issue.
25. Initial Public Offering yields Advice, Firm Commitment, Registration Statement, and Road Show.
# SD1
1. Initial Public Offering from SD zooms in SD1 into Underwriter Selecting, Advice Providing, Fact Evaluating, Registration Statement Preparing, Blue-sky Law Checking, parallel Registration Statement Approving, Issue Price Firming, and Road Show Arranging, Issue Price Fixing, Stock Purchasing, and Stock Offering, which occur in that time sequence.
2. Company is a physical and systemic object.
3. Underwriter Group is a physical and environmental object.
4. Underwriter Group can be candidate or selected.
5. Advice is an informatical and systemic object.
6. Fact Presentation is an informatical and systemic object.
7. Fact Presentation can be fair, presented or unfair.
8. State presented is initial.
9. Registration Statement is an informatical and systemic object.
10. Registration Statement can be approved or pending.
11. State pending is initial.
12. Blue-sky Law Set is an informatical and environmental object.
13. Stock Issue is an informatical and systemic object.
14. Stock Issue can be compliant, new, offered or purchased.
15. State new is initial.
16. Securities & Exchange Commission is a physical and environmental object.
17. Price of Stock Issue is an informatical and systemic object.
18. Price of Stock Issue can be fixed or preliminary.
19. State preliminary is initial.
20. Road Show is an informatical and systemic object.
21. Firm Commitment is an informatical and systemic object.
22. Withdrawal Reason is an informatical and systemic object.
23. Stock Issue exhibits Price.
24. Initial Public Offering is an informatical and systemic process.
25. Underwriter Selecting is an informatical and systemic process.
26. Underwriter Selecting changes Underwriter Group from candidate to selected.
27. Company initiates and handles Underwriter Selecting.
28. Advice Providing is an informatical and systemic process.
29. Underwriter Group handles Advice Providing.
30. Advice Providing yields Advice.
31. Fact Evaluating is an informatical and systemic process.
32. Underwriter Group handles Fact Evaluating.
33. Registration Statement Preparing is an informatical and systemic process.
34. Underwriter Group handles Registration Statement Preparing.
35. Registration Statement Preparing occurs if Fact Presentation is at state fair, otherwise Registration Statement Preparing is skipped.
36. Registration Statement Preparing yields Registration Statement.
37. Blue-sky Law Checking is an informatical and systemic process.
38. Blue-sky Law Checking changes Stock Issue from new to compliant.
39. Underwriter Group handles Blue-sky Law Checking.
40. Blue-sky Law Checking requires Blue-sky Law Set.
41. Registration Statement Approving is an informatical and systemic process.
42. Registration Statement Approving changes Registration Statement from pending to approved.
43. Securities & Exchange Commission handles Registration Statement Approving.
44. Issue Price Firming is an informatical and systemic process.
45. Underwriter Group handles Issue Price Firming.
46. Issue Price Firming affects Price of Stock Issue.
47. Road Show Arranging is an informatical and systemic process.
48. Underwriter Group handles Road Show Arranging.
49. Road Show Arranging yields Road Show.
50. Issue Price Fixing is an informatical and systemic process.
51. Issue Price Fixing changes Price of Stock Issue from preliminary to fixed.
52. Underwriter Group handles Issue Price Fixing.
53. approved Registration Statement initiates Issue Price Fixing, which requires approved Registration Statement.
54. Stock Purchasing is an informatical and systemic process.
55. Stock Purchasing changes Stock Issue from compliant to purchased.
56. Underwriter Group handles Stock Purchasing.
57. Stock Purchasing yields Firm Commitment.
58. Stock Offering is an informatical and systemic process.
59. Stock Offering changes Stock Issue from purchased to offered.
60. Underwriter Group handles Stock Offering.
61. Stock Offering occurs if Withdrawal Reason does not exist, otherwise Stock Offering is skipped.
62. Fact Evaluating changes Fact Presentation from presented to exactly one of fair or unfair.
